### Schedule API Tests - Improved Version
### This file now includes examples with proper User validation and enemy management

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
### Update with actual userId from database
@userId = 5a5bc3b3-6a7c-49d8-8714-f0eeaeee0bf6
@scheduleId = 7bb24d4b-c9b5-44fd-8ce1-8f8ecf559ffe

### ===== STEP 1: GET EXISTING USER_ID =====
### Run this query to see what userIds exist in database
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: application/json

### Copy ID of one user and replace @userId above

### ===== STEP 2: CREATE SCHEDULES =====

### CREATE Schedule - Main variant (pl218 world)
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Daily Farm Schedule",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Main"
}

### CREATE Schedule - Reconnaissance variant (pl219 world)
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Reconnaissance Mission",
  "world": "pl219",
  "scheduleType": "Reconnaissance"
}

### CREATE Schedule - Fake attack
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Fake Attack Training",
  "world": "pl220",
  "scheduleType": "Fake"
}

### ===== STEP 3: FETCHING SCHEDULES =====

### GET all schedules for user
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### GET schedule by ID (replace {{scheduleId}} with ID from response above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{userId}}/{{scheduleId}}
Accept: application/json

### ===== STEP 4: GET TRIBES FOR WORLD =====
### Fetch list of tribes/enemies for schedule's world (cached for 15 minutes)
### Copy tribe IDs you want to set as enemies
GET {{baseUrl}}/worlds/pl218/tribes
Accept: application/json

### ===== STEP 5: SET SCHEDULE ENEMIES =====
### Set enemy tribes for schedule by their TribalWars IDs
### Note: All provided IDs must exist in the world's tribe list
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/enemies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189, 197, 205]
}

### SET ENEMIES - Multiple enemies
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/enemies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189, 197, 205, 210, 215]
}

### SET ENEMIES - Single enemy
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/enemies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189]
}

### SET ENEMIES - Clear enemies (empty list)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/enemies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": []
}

### ===== STEP 6: UPDATE AND DELETE =====

### UPDATE schedule - change to Reconnaissance
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Daily Farm Schedule",
  "world": "pl221",
  "scheduleType": "Reconnaissance"
}

### DELETE schedule (also deletes associated enemies)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}

### ===== INSTRUCTIONS =====
### 1. Run GET /users - you will get list of existing users
### 2. Copy ID of one user (field "id") and replace @userId
### 3. Create a schedule using POST /schedules
### 4. Copy returned schedule ID and replace @scheduleId
### 5. Fetch tribes using GET /worlds/{world}/tribes
### 6. Choose tribe IDs you want as enemies
### 7. Set enemies using PUT /schedules/{scheduleId}/enemies
### 8. GET schedule to verify enemies are set (returned in Enemies field)
### 9. Update/Delete schedule as needed

### Available World values: pl218, pl219, pl220, pl221, pl222, pl223
### Available ScheduleType values: Fake, Reconnaissance, Main
### Note: When setting enemies, all provided TribalWarsIds must exist in the selected world

